# Generated artwork — `node tools/steam-art.mjs` remakes all of it in seconds,
# and it is 9MB of PNG that Vite would never ship anyway (only `public/` is
# copied into `dist`). The tool is the thing worth versioning.
out

# The GIF self-test writes this so a human can eyeball the codec's output; it is
# regenerated by `node tools/gif-selftest.mjs` on demand. The test and encoder
# (tools/gif-selftest.mjs, tools/gif.mjs) are what's worth versioning, not the
# sample they produce. (The shipped help clips live in public/help/ and ARE
# committed — they are the game's imagery, not a test artifact.)
tools/gif-selftest.gif

# Capture rig working files: dumped frames, probe shots, encoded trials.
# The rig writes here by default; KK_SCRATCH points it somewhere else.
tools/capture/.out/
